  "id": "disorders-of-excessive-somnolence",
  "term": "disorders of excessive somnolence",
  "definition": "Disorders of excessive somnolence are conditions marked by unusually strong sleepiness during times when a person would normally be awake, and this can interfere with thinking and mental performance. They include primary hypersomnia conditions as well as forms caused by another known factor, such as substances, mental disorders, or sleep apnea.",
